      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "lack_of_strong_adsorption_sites_on_pore_surface → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] tune pore-surface Lewis base active-site density without changing pore size or pore volume → enables fine tuning of sorption performance without altering confinement effect or sorption capacity associated with pore dimensions"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] replace a pore-surface C-H moiety in MAF-4 with an isoelectronic N atom to create an uncoordinated triazolate Lewis base site → introduces Lewis base active sites for guest binding and significantly enhances sorption performance, especially for more polar adsorbates"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "MAF-47-x vs reported SSF adsorbents: winner=subject_a on ability_to_fine_tune_sorption_without_changing_pore_size_or_volume"
    }
